.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tau 1 31\ Oct\ 2026 tau-lang tau
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtau\fP\fR \fP\fR[\fP\fB\-\-out\-dir\fP\fR=\fP\fIDIR\fP\fR] [\fP\fB\-o\fP\fR=\fP\fIFILENAME\fP\fR] [\fP\fB\-\-crate\-name\fP\fR=\fP\fINAME\fP\fR] [\fP\fB\-C\fP\fR=\fP\fIGEN\fP\fR] \fP\fIPATH\fP
.PP
.SS AVAILABLE\ OPTIONS:
.TP
\fB    \-\-out\-dir\fP\fR=\fP\fIDIR\fP
\fRWrite output to compiler\-chosen filename in DIR\fP
.PP
.TP
\fB\-o\fP\fR, \fP\fB\-\-output\fP\fR=\fP\fIFILENAME\fP
\fRWrite output to FILENAME\fP
.PP
.TP
\fB    \-\-crate\-name\fP\fR=\fP\fINAME\fP
\fRSpecify the NAME of the crate being built\fP
.PP
.TP
\fB\-C\fP\fR, \fP\fB\-\-codegen\fP\fR=\fP\fIGEN\fP
\fRSet the code generator\fP
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h\fP\fR, \fP\fB\-\-help\fP
\fRPrints help information\fP
.PP

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBtau\fR command compiles a Tau source file and generates code using the
specified code generator (e.g., C). Generated files are written to the output
directory, with file extensions determined automatically by the code generator.

If no output directory is specified, the current working directory is used.
If no output name is specified, the input file name is used.

.SH EXAMPLES
Compile a Tau source file:

.EX
tau example/main.tau
.EE

